A shuttle travels around this one-way loop. Edge weights are travel times in minutes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2); \coordinate (B) at (4,2); \coordinate (C) at (4,0); \coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above] {$4$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$3$};
\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,below] {$5$};
\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,left] {$2$};
\draw[->,>=stealth,line width=0.8pt] (1.6,2)--(2.4,2);
\draw[->,>=stealth,line width=0.8pt] (4,1.4)--(4,0.6);
\draw[->,>=stealth,line width=0.8pt] (2.4,0)--(1.6,0);
\draw[->,>=stealth,line width=0.8pt] (0,0.6)--(0,1.4);
\foreach \v/\p in {A/above left,B/above right,C/below right,D/below left}{\fill (\v) circle (2pt) node[\p] {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Calculate the time from $A$ to $D$.
b. Calculate the time for the walk $A\text{–}B\text{–}C\text{–}D\text{–}A\text{–}B$.

The diagram shows travel times in minutes between Home ($H$) and School ($S$).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (H) at (0,1); \coordinate (P) at (2.5,2.3); \coordinate (Q) at (2.5,-0.3); \coordinate (S) at (5,1);
\draw (H)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$7$};
\draw (P)--(S) node[midway,above right] {$9$};
\draw (H)--(Q) node[midway,below left] {$5$};
\draw (Q)--(S) node[midway,below right] {$8$};
\fill (H) circle (2pt) node[left] {$H$}; \fill (P) circle (2pt) node[above] {$P$};
\fill (Q) circle (2pt) node[below] {$Q$}; \fill (S) circle (2pt) node[right] {$S$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Compare $H\text{–}P\text{–}S$ and $H\text{–}Q\text{–}S$. Which is faster, and by how many minutes?

The edge weights are distances in kilometres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,1); \coordinate (B) at (2.5,2.4); \coordinate (C) at (2.5,-0.4); \coordinate (D) at (5,1);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$4$};
\draw (B)--(D) node[midway,above right] {$9$};
\draw (A)--(C) node[midway,below left] {$6$};
\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,below right] {$10$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$3$};
\fill (A) circle (2pt) node[left] {$A$}; \fill (B) circle (2pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2pt) node[below] {$C$}; \fill (D) circle (2pt) node[right] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find a path from $A$ to $D$ with total distance $17\text{ km}$.

Cable segments have latencies in milliseconds. Route $P\text{–}Q\text{–}R\text{–}S$ has total latency $43\text{ ms}$, and route $Q\text{–}R\text{–}T\text{–}U$ has total latency $50\text{ ms}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,1); \coordinate (Q) at (1.8,1); \coordinate (R) at (3.6,1);
\coordinate (S) at (5.4,2); \coordinate (T) at (5.4,0); \coordinate (U) at (7.2,0);
\draw (P)--(Q) node[midway,above] {$12$};
\draw (Q)--(R) node[midway,above] {$x$};
\draw (R)--(S) node[midway,above left] {$15$};
\draw (R)--(T) node[midway,below left] {$y$};
\draw (T)--(U) node[midway,below] {$17$};
\fill (P) circle (2pt) node[left] {$P$}; \fill (Q) circle (2pt) node[below] {$Q$};
\fill (R) circle (2pt) node[above] {$R$}; \fill (S) circle (2pt) node[right] {$S$};
\fill (T) circle (2pt) node[below] {$T$}; \fill (U) circle (2pt) node[right] {$U$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find $x$ and $y$.

A tanker starts at station $A$ and must visit stations $B$, $C$ and $D$ once each. Road distances are in kilometres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (0,2.5); \coordinate (C) at (4,2.5); \coordinate (D) at (4,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$12$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above] {$16$};
\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,right] {$14$};
\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,below] {$23$};
\draw (B)--(D) node[pos=0.3,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$21$};
\fill (A) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$A$}; \fill (B) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$C$}; \fill (D) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Compare the candidate paths $A\text{–}B\text{–}C\text{–}D$ and $A\text{–}B\text{–}D\text{–}C$. Which is shorter?
b. If the tanker uses the first path and then returns directly from $D$ to $A$, find its total distance.
